# {name}

A [supython](https://github.com/your-org/supython) project.

## Quick start

```bash
pip install -e .   # installs this project + supython (pinned in pyproject.toml)
supython up        # start Postgres + PostgREST and apply framework migrations
supython dev       # start the API service on http://localhost:8000
```

`supython init` already generated a ready-to-run `.env` (gitignored) and a JWT
keypair under `.supython/`, so the stack boots with no manual edits. Try the
example function once it's up: `curl http://localhost:8000/functions/hello`.

## Layout

- `{name}/` — your app package: `settings.py`, plus `jobs/` and `hooks/`
  (every module in those packages is auto-imported at boot — see `settings.py`).
- `migrations/` — your application's SQL migrations (e.g. `0001_create_todos.sql`).
  Apply them with your migration tool of choice — [dbmate](https://github.com/amacneil/dbmate)
  is recommended. `supython migrate` applies only supython's own framework
  schemas (auth, storage, realtime, jobs), **not** these.
- `functions/` — edge functions (one `.py` file per route, hot-reloaded).
- `pyproject.toml` — declares this project and pins the supython version.
- `.supython/` — generated JWT keypair, JWKS, and signing secrets. The private
  key and secrets are gitignored; the public JWKS is safe to commit.

## Docs

See the [supython documentation](https://github.com/your-org/supython) for full reference.
